column2:
Mother, in the course of my night
4-5	I walked abroad, brimming with pride, among the young men.
6	The stars of the sky came out for me;
7	a l[u]mp of the sky-rock of Anu fell down at me.
8	I lifted it: it was too heavy for me;
9	I heaved at it: I could not shift it.
10	The land of Uruk gathered about it;
11	the young men were kissing its feet.
12-13	I set my brow to it; they braced with me;
14	I lifted it up and carried it to you.

Likely, Gilgameš, one like yourself
18-19	was born on the open land, and the hills have raised him.
20	You will see him — and you will rejoice;
21	the young men will be kissing his feet;
22-23	you will hug him and lead him here to me.
